[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. The reports say otherwise. Read by
tenant, channel and body, they describe three different failures. Each now has its own ticket
with its own count.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first problem. The form hint and the one-day move stay
broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## The problems in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How they differ

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's date comes
  out with day and month swapped: 7 April arrives as 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3's web form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, even for day-first
  tenants. People type what the hint says, and the form reads it the tenant's way. The swap looks
  the same, but the fix is in the form, not the parser. Only the form channel of booking-v3
  tenants hits it.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by exactly one day, not a swap. The invite arrives before the
  booking; Lisbon and Toronto see different days for one meeting; only June is off. That is a
  time-zone conversion, and no date-order fix touches it. The desk had already read these
  reports as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) but left them filed under the parser.

## Why one ticket hid them

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone, and every one of
these reports says some version of "wrong day". Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's
browser, not their tenant, so it cannot separate them either. The cause is in the tenant's
locale and form, and in the body.

## What changes

- Count each problem on its own ticket. #4471 keeps the parser reports.
- Ship the form hint fix with the parser fix, or booking-v3 tenants keep sending swaps.
- Give the one-day move an owner on the time-zone side.

